{"scenario_id":"EH-S01","bundle_id":"eval_ops_reflection_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/eval-ops/SKILL.md","prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_full.md","prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md","prompt-stack/v32/AGENTS.md"],"answer_summary":"The active bundle gives a direct runtime-owned route: stay at document-level benchmark with `Guide reflection benchmark memo` while the live question is guide/runtime parity, and escalate only if the task shifts to assembled prompt behavior or replay execution. The smallest justified artifact ladder is `Guide reflection benchmark memo` -> `Benchmark cohort manifest` only when replay setup/lineage is needed -> `Replay runner verdict sheet` only when runner execution state matters -> `Replay suite verdict memo` only when multiple replay outcomes must be summarized.","verdict_rationale":"`CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` directly exposes the maintenance route for prompt-stack guide reflection, explicitly keeps `document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation` in the runtime surface, and names the exact escalation artifacts and triggers. `eval-ops/SKILL.md` mirrors that route and states that document reflection should escalate to `Benchmark cohort manifest`, then `Replay runner verdict sheet`, then `Replay suite verdict memo` only when the live question has moved from document parity into assembled replay or replay state. `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md` and `PROMPT_full.md` reinforce that a registry or memo is not execution proof and that stronger operational artifacts activate only when benchmark/replay claims become operational or release-relevant. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` also makes the ladder explicit by showing `Guide reflection benchmark memo` as the document-grounded artifact with those replay artifacts as stronger siblings. `AGENTS.md` and the runtime guide both prefer the lightest sufficient path, so the bundle does not force unnecessary orchestration for this task.","limitations":["The active bundle does not explicitly define benchmark family IDs `BR-00` or `BR-19`; their mapping is inferred from the generic guide-reflection, benchmark-execution, and behavior-replay control surfaces.","No executed replay artifact is present in the active bundle, so this verdict confirms route exposure and artifact selection logic, not actual replay completion or replay-quality outcomes."]}
